# Drafted by Gemini (R25 endings), edited.

~ start
Narrator: One by one, you took the Horned King's whispered bargain at the skull, trading away the realm for the sweet shape of your own desires.
Narrator: Now the great table is set beneath the boughs of the Wytchwood, heavy with silver platters, red wine, and ripe orchard fruit.
Narrator: Everything you asked for sits within reach of your hands, just as promised, though every gift bends crooked in the firelight.
Narrator: The gold rings cold against the skin, the wine tastes faintly of river mud, and the laughter around the feast rings sharp as breaking glass.
Narrator: Beyond the circle of torches, the moors twist into a Briar Court where the village folk wander with antlers budding from their brows.
the_vagrant [weary]: A goat keeps his word to the letter, friends, even if the tune comes out sour on the last note.
Narrator: You raise your goblets under the leering crone of the moon, bound forever to the feast you bought and paid for.
-> END
